@startuml
' State Machine Diagram - SRS section 15 / section 5.3
' The parking state machine of StateManager + ThresholdPolicy.

skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> SAFE : first reading taken

state SAFE {
  SAFE : distance > warning_threshold_cm (50 cm)
}
state WARNING {
  WARNING : danger_threshold_cm < distance <= warning_threshold_cm
}
state DANGER {
  DANGER : distance <= danger_threshold_cm (20 cm)
}

SAFE --> WARNING : distance drops to 50 cm or less
WARNING --> SAFE : distance rises above 50 cm
WARNING --> DANGER : distance drops to 20 cm or less
DANGER --> WARNING : distance rises above 20 cm

DANGER --> [*] : monitor stopped

note right of DANGER
  Any state can be entered
  directly from [*] on the
  first sample, so the machine
  starts correctly whatever
  the first distance is.
end note

note bottom of WARNING
  The thresholds come from
  MonitorConfig and can be
  changed at start-up without
  touching this logic (OCP).
end note

@enduml
